{% extends 'base.html.twig' %}

{% block title %}Composer repository - extdir{% endblock %}
{% block canonical %}<link rel="canonical" href="{{ url('repo_landing') }}">{% endblock %}
{% block meta_description %}extdir's Composer repository, serving metadata for open-source Shopware 6 extensions that are not published on Packagist.{% endblock %}

{% block body %}
<div class="wrap page page--narrow">
    <div class="page-head">
        <p class="eyebrow">For Composer</p>
        <h1>The extdir repository</h1>
    </div>

    <div class="prose">
        <p class="lead">
            A Composer v2 repository for the {{ packages|length }} indexed extensions that are
            <strong>not on Packagist</strong>. Anything Packagist already carries is left out, so
            extdir stays out of your dependency resolution where it adds nothing.
        </p>

        <h2>Using it</h2>
        <pre class="code" tabindex="0"><code>composer config repositories.extdir composer {{ url('repo_landing') }}
composer require vendor/plugin-name</code></pre>
        <p class="small subtle">
            Composer appends <code>/packages.json</code> itself, so the address above has no
            filename on it.
        </p>

        <h2>What it serves, exactly</h2>
        <p>
            Metadata only. Every <code>dist</code> points at the maintainer's release archive or
            GitHub's zipball for the tag, so downloads come from the source. extdir stores no code.
            Read it at <a href="{{ path('repo_root') }}">packages.json</a>, or one package at a time
            at <code>/repo/p2/vendor/name.json</code>.
        </p>
        <p>
            Versions come from git tags. Where <code>composer.json</code> carries a stale
            hardcoded <code>version</code>, the tag wins, which is the rule Packagist applies.
        </p>

        <h2>After installing</h2>
        <pre class="code" tabindex="0"><code>bin/console plugin:refresh
bin/console plugin:install --activate YourPluginName</code></pre>
        <p class="small subtle">
            The technical name is the class in <code>extra.shopware-plugin-class</code>, not the
            package name. Every extension page shows it under <em>Plugin name</em>.
        </p>

        <h2>No lock-in</h2>
        <p>
            Every extension page also shows how to point Composer straight at the source
            repository, with extdir out of the path. This exists because one
            <code>repositories</code> entry beats one per extension. The platform is
            <a href="https://github.com/extdir/extdir">open source</a>.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>
{% endblock %}
